    {
      "id": "claim_b55e91f3a24e49a281d9302b77e3d5f0",
      "statement": "article_score.status SCORED is write-once at the SQL level (its UPDATE branch only fires WHERE article_score.status = 'FAILED'), so a SCORED row can only be overwritten by first deleting it (e.g. a Re-score reset); FAILED increments an attempts counter capped at ArticleScoreStore.MAX_ATTEMPTS=3 retries; SKIPPED is terminal via ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING (first writer wins, no further attempts recorded).",
